# The Dockerfile copies the whole build context, so anything not listed
# here ends up in the image layers, where anyone who pulls the image can
# read it (#163). The image keeps tests/, docs/ and cli/: CI runs pytest
# inside it. The CI build job plants a decoy for each secret/state pattern
# (its DECOYS list) and fails if one leaks: add new patterns to both.

# Secrets and local state
# .env.example holds only placeholders, and the tests load it.
**/.env*
!.env.example
**/*.db*
**/*.sqlite3
**/db.json
data/
uploads/
instance/
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# Development clutter
.git/
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
coverage/
playwright-report/
test-results/
htmlcov/
.coverage
.claude/
.idea/
.vscode/
**/.DS_Store
